    <fr:title text="Retraction Lemma for the Coherence Theorem">Retraction Lemma for the Coherence Theorem</fr:title>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p> Fix a set <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[X]]></fr:tex>. Given a monodial category <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[M]]></fr:tex>, a strong monoidal functor <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[F : M
\to  \mathsf {FreeMon}{\mathopen {}\left (X\right )\mathclose {}}]]></fr:tex>, and an interpretation
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\iota  : X \rightsquigarrow  \mathsf {IsoFiber_{F}}]]></fr:tex> we can use the
<fr:link href="/sss-0064/" title="Global Elimination Principle for the Free Monoidal Category" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-0064/" display-uri="sss-0064" type="local">global elimination principle of the free monoidal category</fr:link>
to construct a global section of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathsf {IsoFiber_{F}}]]></fr:tex>. Then by using the
<fr:link href="/sss-006G/" title="Universal Property of IsoFiber" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-006G/" display-uri="sss-006G" type="local">universal property of IsoFiber</fr:link>, we can extract the
construction of a functor <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[G : \mathsf {FreeMon}{\mathopen {}\left (X\right )\mathclose {}} \to  M]]></fr:tex> such that
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[F \circ  G \cong  \mathsf {Id}]]></fr:tex>.</html:p>
  </fr:mainmatter>
