            <fr:title text="Global Elimination Principle for the Free Monoidal Category">Global Elimination Principle for the Free Monoidal Category</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>Definition</fr:taxon>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>
Given any displayed monoidal category <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[M^{\mathtt {D}}]]></fr:tex> over
<fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathsf {FreeMon}{\mathopen {}\left (X\right )\mathclose {}}]]></fr:tex> with an interpretation <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\iota  :
X \rightsquigarrow  M^{\mathtt {D}}]]></fr:tex>, we may construct a global section <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathsf {FreeMon}{\mathopen {}\left (X\right )\mathclose {}} \to  M^{\mathtt {D}}]]></fr:tex>.
We refer to this as the <html:em>global elimination principle</html:em> of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\mathsf {FreeMon}{\mathopen {}\left (X\right )\mathclose {}}]]></fr:tex>.
</html:p>
